Dear members of LInux-PM list,

We are a development company here in Brazil and used to work with AMD's=20
Geode family processors since it was a NSC product. We have a project=20
for a small terminal and we need some support for the Power Management=20
feature.

We are working with Geode GX1-300MHz and Linux Kernel 2.6.12 (from an=20
Debian distro). We intend to put the cpu under low consuption. The=20
system should come back when it receives an input from the usb=20
interface. The BIOS is compliant with APM 1.2 and ACPI 1.0.

We had success to put the cpu in the suspend mode but we do not know how=20
to come back from an usb (we are working with APM).

I would like to know if some of you could consider some consultant=20
service to help us in this matter. What we need for now is:


1- Decide if APM or ACPI or othe PM system is more adequate for our=20
application;

2- Some documentation regarding how to work with Power Management under=20
Linux with Geode GX1;

3- Remote support helping us to put it to work.

If you have any interest in this task, please contact us ?

We intend to explore the alternatives to have the lowest consuption=20
possible.

